# THE CAPACITY BUFFERS SOMEBODY MEASURED AND FOUND EMPTY, HOWEVER THEY SPELLED IT. One row
# per (filing, layer) whose capacity slack is a measured zero -- as a typed absence or as a
# claim of [0, 0, 0].
#
# ⭐⭐ A SUPPLY THAT CANNOT RUN HOT. If the capacity buffer is empty and somebody checked,
#    then demand above the nameplate CANNOT have been absorbed by running the supply harder.
#    It went unserved, and somebody must be named as having gone without. That is the whole
#    argument the two rules downstream rest on, and it rests on the word "measured": an
#    UNMEASURED capacity slack licenses nothing, because nobody knows whether the supply
#    could have stretched.
#
# ⛔ THE DISJUNCTION IS A UNION OF TWO NAMED RELATIONS RATHER THAN AN `OR` INSIDE A
#   PREDICATE, so each spelling can be run and counted on its own -- and so that adding a
#   third spelling is a file rather than an edit to a condition somebody has to notice.
-- pm:Buffers/pm:Buffer kind="capacity", zero either way.
SELECT z.filing, z.layer, z.absent AS spelled_as_absent, z.high AS spelled_as_claim
FROM (
    :union(ALL entries/zero_by_absence.sqlc, entries/zero_by_claim.sqlc)
) z
WHERE z.buffer = 'capacity'
